# CANONICAL 9B PATH B REFERENCE RUN (coordinator 05:2x, after D1/D2): the rand48 LR-sweep arm B (3e-5) RESUMED from its
# checkpoint (same RUN_NAME) with the RECIPE settings instead of the A-parity ones. Step marker: the first rollout of the
# first chunk of this config (= newest r2 checkpoint + 1, logged by the driver as "resuming LoRA from ...") and every
# later step run under these settings; earlier steps ran swegym-codex-rand48-lora-1n-lr3e-5.env.
# Changes vs the sweep config:
#   * codex window fix (no model_context_window: sessions run to the engine's 64k window, not codex's ~59.1k), ports
#     above 65000, eval-prep race fix (launcher, 9c1da531);
#   * LORA_SERVE=merged (STACK §10: train LoRA, serve merged weights; no LoRA serving flags);
#   * 80 sessions in flight (sweep: 48) on the 2 TP2 engines (1.83M KV tokens each; 48 in flight peaked at 0.38 KV);
#   * eval every 10 steps (sweep: 5); checkpoint every step (sweep: 2); cluster-side chaining (HM_CHAIN_MAX).
# Unchanged: rand48-s0, codex 0.125.0, Qwen3.5-9B, LoRA r32/a64, LR 3e-5, 8 x 8 per step, 64k, overlong = reward 0
# (trained), zero-variance groups dropped, staleness <= 2, trainer TP4 CP1 65536 on 4 GPUs + 2 TP2 engines.
RUN_NAME=swegym-codex-rand48-lora-1n-lr3e-5-r2
HARBOR_TASKS_DIR=${HM_SHARED}/tasks/swegym-lite-v3/harbor
TASK_IDS_FILE=${HM_EXAMPLE_DIR}/configs/swegym-rand48-s0.txt
